{title:BNR one-off report Step 1: Prepare the candidate}

{title:What this step does}

{pstd}
Step 1 packages an analyst-produced final PDF for controlled review. It also
creates the website listing and metadata and can include one complete public
dataset package.

{title:Before you run it}

{pstd}
Finish and inspect the report PDF. Complete the disclosure review appropriate
to the report. If public data accompany the report, prepare the matching CSV,
DTA, YML and README files.

{title:What to enter}

{phang}{bf:Study ID, version and date} define the stable report identity.

{phang}{bf:PDF path, title and description} identify the finished report and
its public listing text.

{phang}{bf:Optional dataset files} must be supplied as a complete set of CSV,
DTA, YML and README files, or all four fields must be left blank.

{phang}{bf:Authorise replacement} should normally remain unticked. A corrected
published report should normally use a higher version.

{title:After running}

{pstd}
Review the complete candidate PDF, landing page, metadata and any dataset ZIP.
When satisfactory, continue to one-off report Step 2.

{title:Full instructions}

{pstd}
See the {browse "https://uwi-bnr.github.io/info-hub/technical/workflows/reporting/one-off-report.html":Technical Manual: Prepare, approve and publish a one-off CVD report}.
